    marks: 15,
    figure: { src: '/exam-figures/maths/mathematics-2024-hl-curve-line-equal-slope.png', alt: 'Coordinate graph on a faint square grid. The x-axis runs from 0 to beyond 10 with labelled ticks at 2, 4, 6, 8 and 10; the y-axis runs from -3 to 3 with labelled ticks at -3, -2, -1, 1, 2 and 3. A smooth S-shaped curve labelled y = p(x) starts near (0, -2·6), dips to a shallow minimum of about -3 near x = 1, rises steeply through roughly (4, 0), reaches a maximum of about 3 near x = 7·5, then turns and falls slightly to about (10, 2·3). A straight line labelled y = l(x) rises gently from about (0, -3) through (6, 0) to (10, 2), giving it a slope of one-half. The curve and line cross at about x = 3·7 and x = 6.', source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Mathematics 2024 Higher Level, Paper 1 Q3(c) — © State Examinations Commission' },
